EXECUTIVE SUMMARY: THE ELIMINATION OF NON-DETERMINISM\uc0\u8232 The Axion Real-Time Stratum (ARTS) is a production-ready, high-performance architectural framework designed to transform standard x86 hardware into a sub-microsecond deterministic engine. Unlike experimental firmware-layer hacks, ARTS operates within the bounds of existing hardware protections while systematically dismantling the overhead of general-purpose operating systems. By leveraging the Linux PREEMPT_RT patchset, Data Plane Development Kit (DPDK), and Intel Resource Director Technology (RDT), ARTS achieves 10/10 stability and performance on Commodity Off-The-Shelf (COTS) hardware. This specification provides the blueprint for hardware-software co-design where jitter is eliminated not by luck, but by structural isolation.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
PHASE I: THE DETERMINISTIC FOUNDATION (RT-KERNEL)\uc0\u8232 The core of ARTS is the replacement of the standard "Completely Fair Scheduler" (CFS) with a deterministic execution environment.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A. PREEMPT_RT Patchset Integration\
ARTS utilizes the Real-Time Linux patchset to make the kernel fully preemptible. This converts almost all kernel spinlocks into sleepable mutexes and moves interrupt handlers into schedulable kernel threads.\
Logic: High-priority user threads can preempt the kernel even during critical sections, ensuring that the "Worst-Case Execution Time" (WCET) is bounded.\
B. Critical Kernel Parameters\
To achieve "Silent Silicon" status, the following boot-time parameters are enforced:\
