PHASE II: CPU TOPOLOGY AND INTERRUPT STEERING\uc0\u8232 ARTS treats the CPU not as a pool of resources, but as a collection of dedicated execution lanes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A. NUMA-Aware Affinity\
To prevent the 30% performance penalty of cross-socket memory access, ARTS binds threads to specific cores within the same NUMA node as the high-speed I/O devices (NICs/NVMe).\
Equation 1: NUMA Locality (L_numa)\
L_numa = (T_local_access / T_remote_access) < 0.5\
By pinning threads via Pthread Affinity, ARTS ensures that L3 cache hits are maximized.\
B. Hardware Interrupt Shielding\
Standard interrupts (IRQs) are the primary cause of jitter. ARTS utilizes the /proc/irq/smp_affinity interface to force all non-essential interrupts (disk, USB, timers) to Core 0, leaving the remaining "Shielded Cores" in a state of pure execution.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
PHASE III: THE ZERO-COPY DATA PATH (DPDK & XDP)\uc0\u8232 Traditional Linux networking (Socket API) is too slow for 10/10 performance due to context switches and memory copies.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A. Kernel Bypass via DPDK\
ARTS implements the Data Plane Development Kit (DPDK). This allows the application to take total control of the Network Interface Card (NIC) via Poll Mode Drivers (PMD).\
Logic: The application continuously polls the NIC hardware ring buffers. Data is moved via DMA directly into the application's memory space.\
Result: Round-trip latency is reduced from 50\'b5s to <2\'b5s.\
B. Hugepages Memory Allocation\
ARTS disables standard 4KB memory paging in favor of 1GB Hugepages. This drastically reduces the size of the Page Table and minimizes TLB (Translation Lookaside Buffer) misses.\
Equation 2: TLB Efficiency (E_tlb)\
E_tlb = (N_huge_hits / N_total_access) -> 1.0\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
PHASE IV: MEMORY HIERARCHY AND CACHE LOCKING\uc0\u8232 To prevent "Cache Pollution" from background tasks, ARTS utilizes hardware-level cache partitioning.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A. Intel RDT / CAT (Cache Allocation Technology)\
Using Intel Resource Director Technology, ARTS assigns specific "Cache Ways" (L3 segments) to the critical process.\
Logic: By masking off portions of the L3 cache via Class of Service (CLOS), ARTS ensures that even if the OS-Ghetto cores become active, they cannot evict the critical data from the CPU's high-speed memory.\
B. Memory Pinning (mlockall)\
To prevent the kernel from ever swapping memory to disk, ARTS uses the mlockall(MCL_CURRENT | MCL_FUTURE) system call. This guarantees that every byte of the ARTS process remains in physical RAM at all times.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
PHASE V: THERMAL AND POWER DETERMINISM\uc0\u8232 Modern CPU power-saving features (C-states/P-states) are the enemies of sub-microsecond stability.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A. Frequency Locking (Maximum Performance)\
ARTS forces the CPU into the "Performance" governor and disables all idle states via the Linux cpupower utility.\
Equation 3: Frequency Stability (F_delta)\
F_delta = F_target - F_current = 0\
By maintaining a constant 4.0GHz+ clock speed, ARTS eliminates the 10-50\'b5s delay associated with the CPU "waking up" from a low-power state.\
B. SMT (Hyper-Threading) Deactivation\
In a 10/10 ARTS environment, Hyper-Threading is disabled at the BIOS/UEFI level. This prevents two threads from competing for the same physical execution units (ALU/FPU), ensuring that execution time is 100% predictable.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
PHASE VI: APPLICATION-LEVEL DETERMINISM\uc0\u8232 Standard C++ or Python libraries often introduce hidden delays. ARTS enforces a "Real-Time Coding Standard."\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A. Lock-Free Architecture\
ARTS strictly forbids the use of mutexes or semaphores in the hot path. Instead, it utilizes Atomic Operations and Single-Producer Single-Consumer (SPSC) Ring Buffers.\
Logic: A thread should never sleep. If data is not ready, the thread continues to poll (Busy-Wait), maintaining its "Hot-Cache" state.\
B. Pre-Allocation Strategy\
Dynamic memory allocation (malloc/new) is prohibited during runtime. All memory, buffers, and objects are pre-allocated during the "Initialization Phase" to avoid the non-deterministic overhead of the glibc allocator.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	8	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
PHASE VII: SYNCHRONIZATION AND TIME-STAMPING\uc0\u8232 To align global clusters, ARTS utilizes hardware-level time synchronization.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A. PTP (Precision Time Protocol)\
ARTS uses IEEE 1588 PTP with hardware timestamping on the NIC. This allows for nanosecond-accurate clock synchronization across multiple servers, accounting for network jitter and cable propagation delays.\
